 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT authorizing the alienation of certain parklands in the town of\nBrookhaven, county of Suffolk",
    "basePrintNo": "S8930",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8930-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Suffolk County",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S8930\n\nSPONSOR: FLANAGAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act authorizing the alienation of certain parklands\nin the town of Brookhaven, county of Suffolk\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo allow authorization from the town of Brookhaven, county of Suffolk,\nto lease certain parklands to the Patchogue-Medford Library.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of this bill provides the provisions for which the Town of\nBrookhaven is authorized to lease to the Patchogue-Medford Library, for\nup to thirty years, and upon such terms and conditions as the town board\ndeems appropriate, the municipality owned parklands.\n\nSection 2 of this bill outlines the stipulations to which Section One of\nthis act shall take into effect in relation to the town of Brookhaven,\ncounty of Suffolk to dedicate an amount equal to the fair market value\nof those interests being transferred by this act, for the acquisition of\nadditional parklands and/or capital improvements to existing park and\nrecreational facilities.\n\nSection 3 of this bill relates to the metes and bounds of the parklands\nauthorized to be leased by the town of Brookhaven, to the Patchogue-Med-\nford Library.\n\nSection 4 of this bill relates to the use of the parkland in the event\nit will cease to be operated as a library.\n\nSection 5 of this bill relates to the parkland in the event it is\nsubject to receive funding pursuant to the federal land and water\nconversation fund. The discontinuance of parklands authorized by the\nprovisions of this act shall not occur until the municipality has\ncomplied with the federal requirements pertaining to the conversion of\nparklands.\n\nSection 6 of this bill is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nTo better address community concerns, the Patchogue-Medford Library\nwould like to construct an annex to their current building to better\naccommodate a higher influx of individuals using their facility. This\nlegislation authorizes the town of Brookhaven to lease parklands to the\nPatchogue-Medford Library as described by the new set of metes and\nbounds contained in this bill.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the State\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
